        "United Muslim Relief demonstrates high operational scale, expanding its financial baseline to <cite id=\"3\">$149,888,609 in FY2024 revenue</cite>. This rapid expansion is backed by <cite id=\"11\">full compliance with all 20 BBB Wise Giving Alliance Standards</cite> and a <cite id=\"1\">94.5/100 rating from Charity Navigator</cite>. Programs are structured around direct aid delivery, allowing the charity to provide essential medical care to <cite id=\"5\">118,908 patients</cite> and reach underserved communities efficiently."
      ],
      "summary": "United Muslim Relief operates as an Above Average global humanitarian organization focused on emergency aid and long-term development. In FY2024, the charity reported <cite id=\"3\">Total Revenue of $149,888,609</cite>, reflecting significant program growth with a <cite id=\"3\">3-Year Revenue CAGR of 191.2%</cite>. The organization holds <cite id=\"1\">a 94.5/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite> and <cite id=\"11\">meets all 20 BBB Wise Giving Alliance Standards</cite>. United Muslim Relief delivers direct aid across multiple regions, reporting that it <cite id=\"5\">served 11,000,000 meals</cite> and <cite id=\"5\">treated 118,908 patients</cite> in recent initiatives. However, donors should note clear financial trade-offs. While the filed Program Expense Ratio is 97.4%, the organization relies heavily on non-cash gifts-in-kind. Its <cite id=\"3\">cash-adjusted program ratio is 48%</cite>, indicating that less than half of cash expenditures directly cover program operations. Additionally, the charity maintains a very thin financial buffer, holding only <cite id=\"1\">0.3 months of working capital in reserve</cite>.",
